1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
AI can finish a student's work
in seconds.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:08,000
ReasonWeave protects what matters:
the learner's thinking.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
They choose, predict, judge evidence,
apply it, create, and revise.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,500
This is a clearly labeled seeded demo.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,500
It is not a live model call.

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:23,500
For learners thirteen and up,
curiosity becomes a source-backed quest.

7
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:28,000
Three methods change
what the learner does.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
When credentialed, GPT-5.6
is configured to create these routes.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,500
The learner still chooses the method.

10
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:40,500
Then they commit to a first model.

11
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:44,000
Evidence stays locked until they do.

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
That preserves the learner's
starting point.

13
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
The AI cannot erase it with an instant
answer.

14
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Now evidence has something
to push against.

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The Evidence Lens keeps its source links.

16
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
It separates evidence from inference
and open questions.

17
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:15,000
When credentialed, live mode admits only
citations returned by OpenAI web search.

18
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
They state what sources establish
and what remains unresolved.

19
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Then they link that finding
to one design choice.

20
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
They build under constraints
and defend tradeoffs.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Visible criteria keep
the task finite.

22
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
The learner—not the AI—
confirms the work.

23
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
They name their prior thinking.

24
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
They show what changed in their model.

25
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
They keep one uncertainty open.

26
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Their words stay separate
from demo feedback.

27
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:03,000
The Curiosity Map replays
the reasoning path.

28
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:08,000
It keeps the learner's
own language visible.

29
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Three questions branch from the model.
The learner chooses what comes next.

30
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Then the portable trace can be
copied and shared.

31
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,000
No grades, accounts, or learner profile.

32
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Four tested server boundaries control
credentialed live generation.

33
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,000
GPT-5.6 plans routes and quests,
then synthesizes evidence.

34
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,500
It grounds feedback and
three next questions.

35
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:38,000
With Codex, evidence judgment became
a product rule.

36
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Codex enforced the design link
and tested the full trace.

37
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Most AI ends curiosity with an answer.

38
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
ReasonWeave makes the thinking visible.

39
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,000
And keeps the human responsible
for the thinking.
